{
 "duration": 25.162,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Emma started at dawn on a grassy trail.",
   "start": 0.3,
   "end": 2.284
  },
  {
   "text": "Every blade was covered in cold dew, and within a mile her cotton leggings were soaked and clinging to her legs.",
   "start": 2.434,
   "end": 8.804
  },
  {
   "text": "Wet cotton stays wet and pulls heat from your body.",
   "start": 9.004,
   "end": 11.91
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the fix. Wear quick-dry nylon pants with a water-repellent finish.",
   "start": 12.31,
   "end": 16.659
  },
  {
   "text": "They shed dew and light drizzle and dry fast once the sun is out.",
   "start": 16.859,
   "end": 20.692
  },
  {
   "text": "Pack a rain shell for real rain.",
   "start": 20.892,
   "end": 22.562
  },
  {
   "text": "Save this before your next morning hike.",
   "start": 22.962,
   "end": 24.962
  }
 ],
